data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":270,"item_id":"fc_03cfe66603deb8aa016adb6c1316608191aa2b89ab1d9fd10a","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"obstacle_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"TASK_INCOMPLETE\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"Lean definition of the source-order scalar-extension module\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Continued by attempting to transport K-scalar multiplication along TensorProduct.comm and type-check a Module K instance on M ⊗[ℤ] K. The probe exposed the right transport direction and confirmed the idea is not yet implemented: the module-field obligations still fail elaboration, notably multiplication-scalar associativity and distributivity over addition. This is unfinished definition work; no mathematical gap is claimed, and no unproved assumption is being added.\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"Actual check_lean_types outputs show the candidate Module instance fails in mul_smul, smul_add, and add_smul. Earlier probes establish the commutor direction K ⊗[ℤ] M ≃ₗ[ℤ] M ⊗[ℤ] K and the prior action type. The exact source target is recorded in source-map.json.\\\",\\\"partial_progress\\\":\\\"Read the source/task/Yui materials and continued using pinned Mathlib APIs. Identified a constructive approach: define source-order scalar action by conjugating the standard K action across TensorProduct.comm, then prove the Module fields. The initial instance probe revealed specific Lean elaboration obligations and was not accepted. A complete interface, plan, and submitted artifact are still absent.\\\"}\"}"}

